@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. It passes this text to print, so render hooks and capturing or buffering work as they do for print.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, process console markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written literally, so brackets and colons are output as-is. It does perform highlighting by default, and accepts a basic ``style``. Set ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off, or ``highlight=True`` to force it even when the console has disabled it. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("[not markup] :smiley:", "foo", sep=" | ", style="bold")
+
+
